Associate, Resource &amp; Capacity Management, GOC

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

As part of the Global Operations Centre (GOC) , you will work closely with teams across the United States, Europe, and Asia to deliver high-impact solutions in a collaborative, multicultural environment. We are looking for an Associate who will:

• Resource allocation and demand support : Support talent allocation and scheduling based on business priorities, skills, availability, utilization and development goals. Review staffing requests, coordinate next steps with managers or senior managers, and identify capacity gaps or allocation conflicts.

• Data accuracy, tracking and reporting : Maintain and validate workforce records, including hires, departures and leave. Prepare staffing reports using Power BI and Excel, ensuring data accuracy and highlighting utilization, capacity and allocation exceptions.

• Stakeholder coordination and employee experience : Coordinate staffing updates with delivery leaders and People teams, supporting onboarding and employee check-ins to understand skills, interests and development goals.

• Process discipline and continuous improvement : Follow staffing governance, documentation and escalation standards while protecting confidential employee and client information. Identify recurring issues, recommend practical improvements, and support the testing and implementation of staffing tools and templates.

Skills and Experience &nbsp;

If this opportunity looks right for you, we are looking for candidates who have:&nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree or equivalent relevant experience in business, HR, operations, analytics, project coordination or a related field.&nbsp;

• Advanced English level (B2-C2).&nbsp;

• Approximately 1 to 3 years in staffing, resource management, operations, HR, project coordination or workforce data; international, matrixed, media or professional-services experience preferred.&nbsp;

• Intermediate Excel skills (formulas, lookups, pivot tables, filters and data validation) and working knowledge of Power BI dashboards.&nbsp;

• Experience maintaining accurate trackers or operational systems; resource management tools are a plus.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

